      "math_academy_id": "e-817",
      "problem": "Find the greatest common factor of the terms $33p$ and $22p.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $33$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 3,\\quad 11,\\quad 33.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $22$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 2,\\quad 11,\\quad 22.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $33$ and $22$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\quad 11.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $11.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Both $33p$ and $22p$ contain $p.$\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $33p$ and $22p$ is $11p.$",
